 "hypothesis_card": {
  "mechanism": "Within an AWS instance family (p4d/p5/...), spot prices across AZs share an administered level set by AWS's spot-pricing algorithm; AZ-level deviations are transient capacity artifacts (reclaimed Capacity Blocks, regional demand spikes). Over 90-180 days the below-median AZs converge up (measured on 2023-06..2024-03 pseudo-origins: up-only shift h180 +0.063 / h90 +0.055 skill vs seed, positive in 7/10 origins, and beating both constant uplift +0.027 and the symmetric form), so adding clip(diff, 0, 0.5) * w (w=0.5 at h90, 0.7 at h180) to the seed's pooled 730-day change quantiles reduces the q50/q90 under-forecast on cheap AZs.",
  "expected_observation": "Discovery pooled skill rises from 0.2450 to ~0.267 (+0.022), with h180 +0.026 and h90 +0.027, h30 unchanged (gated); coverage_80 rises ~+0.022 (fewer q90 breaches on below-median series); median skill +0.017. Dense backtest: pooled +0.022 with z >> 2, ~2/3 of origins improved, helped series concentrated in below-median p4d AZs (use2-az2, apne1-az4, usw2-az3).",
  "competing_explanation": "The gain is not cross-sectional mean reversion but a generic upward center shift that happens to look good in the 2023-24 AI-demand Discovery window (any uplift would score well while prices rose); alternatively it is pure variance reduction from shrinking the gap to the family median. Evidence against the rival: constant uplift (+0.10/+0.20 log) scored only +0.027 h180 vs up_only's +0.063 on the same pseudo-origins, and the down-only direction was Discovery-NEGATIVE (-0.019 h180, dry run 1) \u2014 a generic \"prices rose\" artifact would have rewarded both directions.",
  "test": "Paired dry run on the 16 Discovery origins (pooled +0.0225, 10/16 origins improved, h90 +0.027 / h180 +0.026, coverage +0.022) plus a dense 33-origin stride-14 backtest inside Discovery (pooled delta +0.0219, origin-bootstrap SE 0.0027, z = 8.0, 64% of origins improved, helped cells concentrated in below-median p4d AZs, worst regression -0.003 on a single p5 series). The direction was decided by a pseudo-origin scan restricted to the scored window after the down-only variant failed the screen (-0.009 pooled).",
  "rejection_condition": "Rejected if Discovery pooled skill <= champion (0.2450) or any sanity check fails (final: 0.2675, screen PASS). The reversion hypothesis is falsified if the h90/h180 gains do not transfer out of sample (Holdout h90 <= 0.2150 or h180 <= 0.3551, the champion's values) or if the dense backtest delta is not significant (|z| < 2); measured z = 8.0, so only a Holdout reversal would falsify it."
